  "upstream": [
    "CVE-2026-15176"
  ],
  "published": "2026-10-23T23:35:05Z",
  "modified": "2026-10-23T23:35:05Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow via post-rewrite URI to path\n     mapping with alias\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-15176.patch: in ngx_http_map_uri_to_path(),\n       reject the mapping for a location using \"alias\" when r->uri_changed is\n       set, so a rewritten URI shorter than the location prefix is no longer\n       mapped to a path (e.g. via $request_filename)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-15176-2.patch: in ngx_http_script_break_code(),\n       clear r->valid_location when the URI was changed, so the alias check\n       also rejects the mapping after a standalone \"break\"\n     - CVE-2026-15176",
